From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:28:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] usb: dwc2: Do not clear the receive buffer before every
 packet

Each bulk OUT packet of at most 512 bytes first filled XFER_SIZE (16 KiB) of
the endpoint's buffer with 0xaa, over its 4 KiB share of the DMA page and into
the buffers of the endpoints after it. Nothing reads those bytes: the
transfer's completed size says how much data arrived.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/usb_dwc2.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/usb_dwc2.c b/src/usb_dwc2.c
index 9220d62..7922bc4 100644
--- a/src/usb_dwc2.c
+++ b/src/usb_dwc2.c
@@ -1003,7 +1003,6 @@ static void usb_dwc2_cdc_start_bulk_out_xfer(dwc2_dev_t *dev, u8 endpoint_number
     if (ringbuffer_get_free(host2device) < XFER_SIZE)
         return;
 
-    memset(dev->endpoints[endpoint_number].xfer_buffer, 0xaa, XFER_SIZE);
     usb_dwc2_ep_hw_recv(dev, endpoint_number, 512, 1);
     dev->endpoints[endpoint_number].xfer_in_progress = true;
 }
